     "q": "This was the original gold code. Which line makes the alerts disappear?",
     "code": "out = (events.join(prev, \"engine_id\", \"left\")\n       .groupBy(\"engine_id\").applyInPandas(_fold, OUT_SCHEMA)\n       .persist())\nmerge_state(out.filter(\"kind = 'state'\"))\nmerge_alerts(out.filter(\"kind = 'alert'\"))",
     "a": 3,
     "why": "`.persist()` doesn't guarantee the cached result is reused. The second action can recompute `out` after state was updated. Use `.localCheckpoint(eager=True)` and write alerts first.",
